🟠 node-local-dns in kube-system (prod-eu-1) keeps crashing because it holds the resolver address their lookups time out on. It fails with "[FATAL] listen tcp 169.254.20.10:8080: bind: address already in use". Replicas that do not depend on it are healthy. Affected: invoices in billing; transcode in media; web in shop. To read the output of the last crash, run kubectl logs ds/node-local-dns -c app -n kube-system --previous
